A file can be deleted and a document can be trashed. The correct rendering of an edge to
something gone is a **visible dangling link** — never a crash, and never a silent
create. An unreachable drive, a refused capability and a missing file all degrade to the
same honest state: the link still renders, marked unresolved.

That is tested directly, because a workspace that breaks when a drive is down is not a
workspace with links — it is a workspace with a dependency.

